# Starnik first (then Drukarnik / hunspell)

Never lock a common lemma from memory, from the Russian shape, or by
blind string replace. Open the page and read it.

## What each tool is for

| Tool | Use for | Do not use for |
|------|---------|----------------|
| **Starnik** `https://starnik.by/pravapis` | **Sense** (numbered glosses + examples) and the **case/conjugation table** | Final tarask spelling when it clashes with hunspell |
| **Liza** `https://starnik.by/lizabeta` (UI/IT EN→BE) | UI verbs like Cancel→Скасаваць; “як не перакладаць” | General prose synonyms |
| **Drukarnik** `https://drukarnik.app/` | Second pass: word forms, IT glossary (Liza moved here), catch Russian `и` / bad endings in a phrase | Replacing `hunspell -d be_BY@tarask` (project gate stays tarask) |
| **Skarnik** | Only if RU→BE mapping is still unclear after Starnik | Skipping Starnik |
| **hunspell** `be_BY@tarask` | Spelling gate in this repo | Meaning / which synonym |

- Meaning: Starnik wins.
- Spelling clash with tarask hunspell: hunspell wins (`шкіпэр`, `дэпазыт`).
- UI/IT English labels: Liza / Drukarnik IT glossary.
- TERMBASE `source`: Starnik `/pravapis/<id>` URL when the word is there.

## Starnik workflow (every new or changed lemma)

1. Name the **Russian sense in this UI line** (not “first gloss in the dict”).
2. Open `https://starnik.by/pravapis?q=<lemma>` (search), or a known
   `/pravapis/<id>` link. Homographs: pick the sense that matches the UI.
3. Read the **definition and examples**, then the **declension /
   conjugation table**. Copy the ending you need (N/G/D/A/I/L), not a
   look-alike from Russian (`клан`: G **клана**, D **клану** — do not
   keep Russian `-у` genitive).
4. Belarusian has **і**, not Russian **и**. If a BE cell has `и` outside
   a proper name or an intentional broken-RU joke, it is wrong.
5. Do not keep the Russian shape because it “looks close”
   (`корсар` → `карсар`).
6. Run `hunspell -d be_BY@tarask` on the form. Spelling clash → hunspell.
7. Optional: paste the phrase into Drukarnik and check forms / IT terms;
   still verify sense on Starnik before changing the corpus.
8. Write/update `TERMBASE.tsv`: sense, endings actually used, rejected
   calque, Starnik URL.

## Anti-patterns (already burned us)

- Global `клян`→`клан` without re-checking the **case** in each line.
- Treating a rejected-form hit as “replace the substring” without reading
  Starnik sense (e.g. fish `плаўнік` ≠ diving `ласты`).
- Using Drukarnik/Skarnik/hunspell alone and skipping the Starnik sense.
